—At that same moment, at the Royal Guest House in the royal capital of Lugunica.

This day was supposed to mark the starting point of an event of immense significance—both for the Kingdom of Lugunica and for the camp of Emilia, the royal selection candidate.

A golden opportunity to eliminate the lingering curse of the Witch's Cult's disaster that had struck the Watergate City of Priestella. That moment, which was to be realized with the cooperation of the Holy Dragon Church—Emilia and the others were to be present, witnessing the wiping away of months of helplessness. That had been the plan.

"—So, in light of all that, what exactly is the meaning of this situation?"

The preparations for departure had been completed. All that remained was to wait for Subaru and Beatrice, who had left the residence on an errand, to return. Amidst that lull, with the camp enjoying teatime in the reception room, Otto Suwen posed the question, striving to remain calm, to the sudden visitors.

Barging into the Royal Guest House with great clamor and fanfare were royal soldiers, all equipped in a manner indicating their official affiliation with the kingdom. Guarding the women, including Emilia, from the soldiers who exuded a somewhat heavy, tense atmosphere, Otto stepped forward.

Of course, standing even further forward than Otto was—

"That's a pretty rough way to act, ain't it. No matter how much Lady Emilia is all gentle an' soft, that don't give you lot permission to go 'round bein' rude."

"Garfiel, don't intimidate them too much. They are guests. —For now."

"Got it, Otto-nii."

With a token effort at pacifying Garfiel, who stood at the very front of the camp gnashing his sharp fangs, Otto created a pause to make the other party state the reason for their visit.

It was a bit of a set-up, but a deliberate move to cede the initiative and position things as a favor owed.

If, at the very least, they understood that—

"—All of you, restrain your fighting spirit. Do you understand who stands before you?"

The moment that low voice rang out, every royal soldier spread throughout the reception room straightened their posture in perfect unison. Slipping through the cordon of now-ramrod-straight soldiers, making heavy, lumbering footsteps as he approached, was a towering man of massive build.

Clad head-to-toe in armor shining with a steel-like gleam, the owner of that craggy, boulder-like face was the Captain of the Royal Guard of the Kingdom of Lugunica—in other words, the man standing at the very pinnacle of the kingdom's knights, Marcos Gildark.

"Marcos-san..."

"I deeply apologize for this sudden visit, Lady Emilia."

At the sight of Marcos stepping forward, Emilia blinked her violet eyes. In response to her reaction, Marcos—in stark contrast to his rugged appearance—offered a bow that perfectly followed every point of etiquette.

Then, raising his head, he fixed his eyes on Emilia and everyone in the camp surrounding her, his gaze particularly stern as he looked upon Otto and Garfiel.

"The reason we have called upon you in this manner is to request that Lady Emilia present herself at the royal castle. There is an urgent matter of doubt that must be verified without fail."

"This is terribly abrupt. A matter of doubt? Whatever could that be..."

"—It concerns the background of the knight, Natsuki Subaru."

"Subaru's?"

Marcos adhered to etiquette, showed respect, and yet his attitude brooked no refusal. Hearing that the matter of doubt he spoke of was connected to Subaru, Emilia reacted with words, while Otto and the others all responded with varying expressions and shifts in posture.

Otto would later regret that this had created an opening for Marcos to speak his next words.

For the matter of doubt related to Natsuki Subaru that Marcos pronounced was—

"The knight, Natsuki Subaru, is suspected of having strong ties to the Witch's Cult—to the extent of being akin to an Archbishop of the Deadly Sins."

—A watershed moment that would determine whether Natsuki Subaru was to be deemed an enemy of the world.




